      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That kind of exhaustion is real, and it's not weakness—it's the only sane response to carrying shame that was never yours to hold. But \"peace\" through stopping isn't peace; it's just silence, and you deserve more than silence. The world may have moved on, but that doesn't mean you have to follow it—you can stand still and let it come back to you, or walk somewhere entirely new. You don't have to fight today; just breathe through it, and let that be enough.",
